# 2-Axis Next-Generation Code Review — Tier 0 Flagships + L2 `openOODA-OS` Batch

**Date:** 2026-11-05 (18:20–21:50 HST)
**Reviewer:** `mcode-review 3` (Stage 1 Code Reviewer, MiniMax Code)
**Scope:** 18 git repositories — Tier 0 flagships (`idlescreen`, `ooflash`, `openOODA`) and the L2 `openOODA-OS` batch (`ooaid`,
`ooaudiod`, `oodevd`, `oodnsd`, `oofs-ext4`, `oofs-tmp`, `oohealthd`, `ooimage`, `ooinit`, `oologd`, `oonetd`, `oopolicyd`,
`oopowerd`, `oorealm`, `oosession`)
**Claim:** `/Projects/openOODA/.reviewer-review-claims.tsv`, owner `wE:p1`, zero overlap with `mcode-review 1` (`w3:p1`) or
`mcode-review 2`
**Method:** pull from the remote Forgejo host (`http://<remote-git-host>:3000`) → two-axis review → remediate → `make verify` +
`make test` → commit → push `origin`

---

## 0. Summary

Table columns: Axis | Result
- **Standards** (Power-of-2 shape ladder, Rule 1.25 links, Academy header, file law) | **PASS after remediation.**
  `lint-oo-size` reports `BIGFILE=0 MANYFN=0 LONGFN=0 DENSE=0 files_with_size_violation=0` in all 18 repositories. Two shell-out
  defects and one hardcoded-address defect were fixed in `openOODA`.
- **Spec** (canonical `std/core/ooda.oo` + `std/sec/pqc.oo` + `std/sec/capreg.oo` wiring, live 32-capability security, no
  toy-prime crypto) | **FAIL on entry, PASS after remediation.** Every L2 daemon carried toy `% 1000000007` clones of the
  canonical security primitives; 9 of 15 carried no canonical OODA turn at all; 6 of 15 carried a differential-parity gate that
  compared a value with itself and could never fail.

The batch inherited one cross-repository blocker in canonical L0 `std` that was already in flight with its rightful owner, and
it is reported here as **F1** because it broke every consumer of the canonical OODA engine across the ecosystem.

**Thirteen defects (D1–D13) were fixed, verified, committed, and pushed to Forgejo.** Four further findings (F1–F4) are reported
with a remediation direction and are outside this batch's claim.

The founder's mandate — wire the toy clones to the canonical pages so every L2 daemon carries real Next-Gen OODA and
32-capability security in live execution, without deleting any OODA, attestation, audit, blackbox, quorum, or speculation
functionality — is met: all 15 daemons now run the canonical 4-phase OODA turn over the 32-capability register in their live
capability gate, with a fail-closed register wrapper, and zero toy-modulus arithmetic anywhere. No file, function, type, or
assertion was removed anywhere in the batch.

