### 1.2 Rule 1.25 link law, conflict markers, banned file names

Every repository was scanned for symbolic links and for hard links (`find -type l`, `find -type f -links +1`, excluding `.git`),
for merge conflict markers across `.oo`, `.oot`, `.md`, and `Makefile`, and for the banned file-name list (`util.oo`, `utils.oo`
, `helper.oo`, `helpers.oo`, `common.oo`, `misc.oo`, `shared.oo`, `base.oo`, `core.oo`).

**Zero links, zero conflict markers, zero banned names in all 18 repositories.**

### 1.3 Academy header

The Academy gate is the repository's own `make academy` target, which scans `head -16` of every `.oo` page for `// # `,
`// Logline:`, `// Setup:`, and `// Beats:`. `idlescreen` and every L2 daemon run it inside `make verify`, and all report
`PASS: academy headers hold`.

`openOODA` has no root `Makefile`; its Academy and shape gates run through `.github/workflows/ci.yml`, which builds
`qa/lint_oo_size.oo` and runs the polyrepo inventory. The inventory reports `files_with_size_violation=0` for the 665 pages of
the governance repository.

